## Partials

Two ways of drawing a history read by symfony-activity's `ActivityRepository`, to include in a page of the application:

```twig
{# The last entries, newest first, as a timeline, with the way to the rest. #}
{% include '@WexampleSymfonyActivityDsBundle/partials/recent.html.twig' with {
    entries: activity_repository.findRecent(subject, 10),
    more_href: path('history_page'),
} %}

{# One page of it as a table, and its pages: the array ActivityRepository::paginate() returns, with the current page. #}
{% include '@WexampleSymfonyActivityDsBundle/partials/table.html.twig' with {
    entries: found.entries, page: page, pages_count: found.pages_count,
} %}
```

Each entry shows its category, its type code, its time and its context as recorded; one done by someone else than the subject says so. A failure, a refusal, a denial or an expiry is drawn in the danger tone. The page including them imports the styles of the `timeline`, `data-table`, `pagination` and `marker` components.

The account pages of symfony-user-ds use both: the recent block on `/accounts/{id}`, the table on `/accounts/{id}/activity`.
